[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The joints and the language over them

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-FLOWS
TITLE: The joints and the language over them
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
STATEMENT: >>>
The operations logic can attach to, what a handler sees, and the open decisions on shape.

- The hook layer's joints are the before and after of each operation: scribe's command, load, change (create, delete, set, unset, relate, unrelate, move), write, reload and read; git's commit (before, message, after), push (before), and rewrite, merge and checkout (after); and strictdoc's index (after). [WORKS]
- A handler receives the operation, its phase, the actor when known, and a payload (node, kind, field, old and new value — or a ref range for git). It returns 0 to let the operation proceed, 1 or a refusal to stop it; any other return value is a bug. [WORKS]
- Three hook-layer capabilities are unbuilt: the actor slot, the old value on a field change, and a typed refusal. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-IDENTITY-HAS-NO-CARRIER]. [GAP]
- The hook layer waits on three decisions: how fine-grained the joints are, where non-hook settings live, and whether triggers are strings or typed. See [LINK: DEC-HOOK-GRANULARITY], [LINK: DEC-HOOK-SETTINGS-NAMESPACE] and [LINK: DEC-HOOK-TRIGGER-REPRESENTATION]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [OPEN: DEC-HOOK-GRANULARITY, DEC-HOOK-SETTINGS-NAMESPACE, DEC-HOOK-TRIGGER-REPRESENTATION]
- The semantic layer's language waits on two decisions: its shape — Jira-style transitions, XState-style machines, or admission rules — and whether one or two layers sit between the hooks and the language. See [LINK: DEC-DSL-LAYER-COUNT] and [LINK: DEC-DSL-SHAPE]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [OPEN: DEC-DSL-SHAPE, DEC-DSL-LAYER-COUNT]
- Conditions are JsonLogic trees, typed in Nix, evaluated in Python at the joint over the node, its one-hop neighbours and the acting identity. [WORKS]
- Creating a node touches disk even under dry-run, so a 'before the write' joint already sees a file. [GAP]
- Signing is a standalone script today, the only thing that writes fingerprints, with no scribe verb. Dissolved into a scribe operation on the fingerprint field plus a semantic-layer gate on readiness and class. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-SEMANTICS-LIVE-IN-TOOLS-WITH-NO-OWNER] and [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-IDENTITY-HAS-NO-CARRIER]. [FALLS OUT: a scribe move on PARENT_FP + L3 gate (readiness + class)]
- CI runs one command, a named gate. Automatic transitions are reported as due, never fired. [WORKS]
- Handover to beads and a board over it: the board sits over the execution engine, not the plan. Whether the board shows plans or work, and whether the viewer is a terminal or the web, are undecided — the direction presumes a terminal. See [LINK: DEC-TUI-BOARD-SUBJECT] and [LINK: DEC-VIEWER-FORM-UNDECIDED]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [OPEN: DEC-TUI-BOARD-SUBJECT, DEC-VIEWER-FORM-UNDECIDED]
- Merge and rewrite fire only afterwards, and a textual merge can produce a state no transition would have. The gate catches that state but cannot name the transition that should have happened. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MERGE-BOUNDARY-IS-NOT-A-JOINT]. [WORKS]
- The emitted model carries a version. What it is compared to, and what fails on a mismatch, is unwritten. [GAP]
- Hook settings would mount under the strictdoc option tree, which cannot be exported as a devenv facet. [UNADDRESSED]
<<<
